<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34154" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pā^trĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		patria. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to one's native
				country</i> or <i>home</i>, <i>native</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">patrius sermo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 1, 2, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor.
				A. P. 57</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Par. 4, 1, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Leg. 2, 9, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">carmen patrium canere,</span>”
				<i>a national song</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Curt.
					3, 3, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mycenae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>their home</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 180</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palaestrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 281</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2
					Macc. 7, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., in gram.: nomen patrium, <i>a gentile
			noun</i> (like Romanus, Atheniensis, etc.),
				<i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 580</span></i> P.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
